WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:18.000
England's Day of Days. Westminster Abbey is the setting for the shore of the century as peers arrive for the coronation of King George VI.

00:18.000 --> 00:25.000
The Archbishop of Canterbury who is to crown the King.

00:25.000 --> 00:32.000
From Britain's far-flung dominions come their premiers.

00:32.000 --> 00:39.000
Members of the royal family come to play their roles in this glittering pageant.

00:39.000 --> 00:43.000
And the great crowd surging around the Abbey hailing with fervor.

00:43.000 --> 00:49.000
The carriage of state bring the Princess Royal and the Duchesses of Gloucester and of Kent.

00:49.000 --> 00:59.000
The arrival of the royal family is the signal for frenzied cheering from the crowd.

00:59.000 --> 01:04.000
The Queen Mother who is their queen for so many years is the idol of the British public.

01:04.000 --> 01:07.000
While the little princesses have captured every heart.

01:07.000 --> 01:14.000
Today is their big day of days too and they're enjoying every minute of it in round-eyed childish wonderment.

01:14.000 --> 01:33.000
The big moment the crowd's been waiting for.

01:33.000 --> 01:38.000
The King and Queen leave Buckingham Palace on their way to the Abbey in the famous coach of state.

01:38.000 --> 01:46.000
The ornate golden carriage with its crystal windows, its colourful postilions and its superb orchette of match grey horses.

01:46.000 --> 01:57.000
This coach built in 1761 is the symbol of regal pomp and ceremony.

01:57.000 --> 02:01.000
The route of their majesties in their striking military escort.

02:01.000 --> 02:08.000
The King's fighting men from all over the world is along the mall to Trafalgar Square and through Whitehall to the Abbey.

02:08.000 --> 02:12.000
And it's one prolonged roar for the entire two miles.

02:12.000 --> 02:14.000
The roar of the British lion.

02:14.000 --> 02:19.000
Hundreds of thousands of folks in a roar of welcome and of allegiance.

02:19.000 --> 02:23.000
Hour after hour the crowds have waited to see this great pageant of empire.

02:23.000 --> 02:26.000
Many of them for 15 or 18 hours.

02:26.000 --> 02:37.000
And now their reward, the King and his beautiful Queen on their way to the coronation.

02:37.000 --> 02:52.000
The roar rises to a deafening din of cheers and exultant shouts of long live the King as the stagecoach nears the Abbey.

02:52.000 --> 02:59.000
The crowds masked here have seen piers and piruses, foreign potentates and visiting dignitaries from the four corners of the globe.

02:59.000 --> 03:04.000
But this is the supreme thrill.

03:04.000 --> 03:11.000
Like figures out of a storybook, the regal pair with their elaborate state robes of satin, of velvet and of miniver,

03:11.000 --> 03:16.000
leave their golden carriage for the next impressive act in this great dynastic drama.

03:16.000 --> 03:27.000
While in their ears ring an unprecedented ovation, ample proof of the popularity they enjoy.

03:27.000 --> 03:32.000
And now inside the Abbey comes the crowning of George VI.

03:32.000 --> 03:42.000
George VI, his most excellent majesty by the grace of God of Great Britain, Ireland and of the British dominions beyond the seas.

03:42.000 --> 03:48.000
King, defender of the faith, Emperor of India.

03:48.000 --> 03:54.000
Eight thousand have crowded this old Abbey to witness the ceremony that is as old as England's kings.

03:54.000 --> 03:59.000
The royal family, peers of the realm, foreign royalty and all the nobility of Europe,

03:59.000 --> 04:20.000
here are gathered dignitaries from far countries, from the reaches of the empire, all to swear fealty to a new sovereign.

04:20.000 --> 04:22.000
Breathtaking is the word for the ceremony.

04:22.000 --> 04:29.000
Eighty million dollars worth of jewels are on display here. The crown jewels alone are valued at thirty millions of dollars.

04:29.000 --> 04:35.000
A fitting background to a ceremony of pomp and circumstances that is unparalleled by any other people's.

04:35.000 --> 04:45.000
Pageantry that is England's own, unchanged through the centuries.

04:45.000 --> 04:54.000
So it's Hail George VI, and throughout the empire upon which the sun never sets, there's occasion for wild celebration.

04:54.000 --> 05:06.000
God save the king.

05:06.000 --> 05:12.000
The triumphant procession back to Buckingham Palace is the most spectacular military display on record.

05:12.000 --> 05:18.000
Miles of troops and carriages, picked troops from every part of the world, from every fighting unit in the empire,

05:18.000 --> 05:24.000
in a bewildering variety of uniforms and equipment, here to do honor to their new liege lord,

05:24.000 --> 05:32.000
to show the world that the line of empire still girdles the earth.

05:32.000 --> 05:42.000
Premier Mackenzie King of Canada with his striking escort of Royal Mounties.

05:42.000 --> 05:47.000
The little princesses ride with their grandmother during the tumultuous procession back to the palace.

05:47.000 --> 05:49.000
What a day it has been for them.

05:49.000 --> 05:59.000
But there's more excitement ahead as the glittering parade winds its way through crowded London streets.

05:59.000 --> 06:04.000
And now the man on the street is to get his first chance to hail the new sovereigns as king and queen

06:04.000 --> 06:09.000
in all their regal array of jewels and gold, of ermine and royal purple,

06:09.000 --> 06:14.000
as they leave Westminster for their spectacular journey to Buckingham, a journey of state.

06:14.000 --> 06:19.000
And so that a million or more of their loyal subjects, jammed by the hundreds of thousands along the Four Mile Route,

06:19.000 --> 06:26.000
may see them in their splendor, the coach is specially lighted so they can plainly see their majesties.

06:26.000 --> 06:39.000
And what a cheer of loyalty they get.

06:39.000 --> 06:53.000
At Trafalgar Square the crowd literally goes wild as the royal carriages pass.

06:53.000 --> 06:57.000
One of the most interesting groups in the parade, of course, is the famous Yeoman of the Guard,

06:57.000 --> 07:06.000
the beef eaters of song and story.

07:06.000 --> 07:13.000
Rain, off and on during the parade, failed to dim the color or lessen the snap of the famous units in the line of march.

07:13.000 --> 07:17.000
Nor did it dampen the enthusiasm of the cheering thousands on the sidelines.

07:17.000 --> 07:30.000
The troops lined the street shoulder to shoulder every foot of the way.

07:30.000 --> 07:35.000
Nations of all the world are represented in the procession, in carriages, cars, or on horseback,

07:35.000 --> 07:43.000
a tribute of courtesy to the newly crowned monarch of one quarter of the globe.

07:43.000 --> 07:53.000
Without doubt, the coronation and this magnificent procession is one of the greatest displays ever presented.

07:53.000 --> 08:01.000
The show nears its end as the famous Golden Coat, with its escort of male lifeguards and others, enters Hyde Park.

08:01.000 --> 08:21.000
This most brilliant of pageants approaches its finale as the state coach arrives back at Buckingham Palace.

08:21.000 --> 08:29.000
And a grand finale it is, with still more countless thousands massed before the palace to assure the new king of their loyalty and devotion.

08:29.000 --> 08:48.000
Soon they'll send up their voices in a mighty roar for the king and queen to appear on the balcony, a sort of curtain call after the historic drama.

08:48.000 --> 08:52.000
Called unexpectedly to the throne by a sudden twist of fate,

08:52.000 --> 09:01.000
George VI becomes the 40th British sovereign at the age of 41. With his happy family around him is today's man of destiny,

09:01.000 --> 09:21.000
an arbiter of the destiny of 500 million people. Long may he reign.

09:21.000 --> 09:23.000
You

